Author: Peyton Montei <peyton@entire.io>
Date:   Wed Aug 12 17:06:02 2026 -0700

    feat(settings): add exclude_paths_exact and polish the global gate API

    Add exclude_paths_exact to GlobalConfig: plain paths (no glob support)
    excluded exactly, with no subtree cascade — an entry matches only when
    it IS the worktree root. This closes the home-as-dotfiles-repo gap: a
    bare exclude_paths dir pattern deliberately excludes its whole subtree,
    so there was no way to exclude exactly $HOME without excluding every
    repo beneath it, and no-origin repos can't use exclude_origins either.
    Entries follow the same discipline as exclude_paths: TrimSpace,
    blank-skip, tilde expansion, platform case folding, symlink-robust
    comparison, and fail-closed on unusable entries (relative, ~user).

    API polish from review:
    - document the load-bearing nil-means-unconfigured invariant on
      UserSettings.Global itself, not just on the loader
    - stop re-probing IsSetUpAny inside IsActiveForRepo: IsSetUpAndEnabled
      re-ran the Lstat pair the gate had just paid; extract
      repoSettingsEnabled and call it directly
    - extract rootMatchForms, shared by the glob and exact matchers

